            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Judy Hidy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent, but I prefer using all brown sugar. Strange, but in this recipe the curry tastes more like nutmeg than curry. I also like to add a few toasted pecans on top of this dish just before serving. Judy"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "janice"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My grandmother-in-law used to make this and I always enjoyed it. I like to make this for Thanksgiving dinner and to go with pork tenderloin. When I make this I like to use dried apricots because I don’t think canned have very much flavor, I reconstitute them overnight in the juice from the canned pears. I also use dried cherries as I think maraschino don’t taste like cherries.",
            "datePublished": "2022-02-26T01:43:59.383Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nancyjo53"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We brought this to a Church Handbell Christmas party, and it was a hit. I could not find an apricot canned, dried or fresh so I used canned whole cranberries and it was still excellent. I would like to try it by also adding an extra cup of some kind of dried fruit.",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-05T03:40:05.389Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sligo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My mom always made this to go with holiday ham, and it's been a family favorite for over 50 years. I use all brown sugar. Make sure the fruit is very well drained. I melt the butter and sugar and then add curry and stir with the fruit and bake. Great the next day.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-22T02:35:00.527Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PerkyStew3989"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My family has made this as a warm side for the Christmas ham for almost 60 years. It is especially pretty for the holidays when made with the maraschino cherries. Definitely better the next day, too!",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-25T02:08:12.203Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Loulala"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made my own version of this recipe for many years and love it. One can vary the curry from mild to hot, based on personal taste. It is always better a day after cooking so do ahead and reheat. I like it with dried apricots, not fresh. I serve over rice, with chicken, pork or turkey.",
            "datePublished": "2015-08-12T05:39:18.460Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jennice"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is the perfect holiday side dish. Like previous reviewers, I used all brown sugar instead of white. It's even better the next day.",
            "datePublished": "2015-01-04T14:05:53.590Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RSHEAHAN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "MMM! I looked for this recipe because I remembered it fondly from a potluck breakfast brunch back in the mid 70s. I recreated it from this recipe for our Christmas dinner at work. My fellow workers are not adventurous but it was well received. I didn't care if they like it or not - more for me!",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-27T19:39:38.917Z"
          },
          {
